1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,205
Vanakkam. This is Liam, in for Bear, with chapter one of INFO 7375, Computational

2
00:00:04,225 --> 00:00:08,732
Skepticism for AI, at Northeastern. This film is about one test for any claim about

3
00:00:08,752 --> 00:00:13,561
a model: what result would make it false? A claim counts only if it names that

4
00:00:13,581 --> 00:00:18,088
result. You'll see each claim drawn as the outcomes it forbids. The trap: a claim

5
00:00:18,108 --> 00:00:21,710
nothing could refute looks, on a dashboard, just like one that passed.

6
00:00:21,780 --> 00:00:26,275
Why should you care? Every model you ship or buy arrives with claims like robust,

7
00:00:26,295 --> 00:00:30,789
performs well, a success. If a claim forbids nothing, no test can ever catch the

8
00:00:30,809 --> 00:00:34,702
model failing. A sepsis model passed every check its builders chose, and still

9
00:00:34,722 --> 00:00:38,915
missed roughly two in three septic patients. Write the forbidden result first, and a

10
00:00:38,935 --> 00:00:40,420
test can finally say no.

11
00:00:40,490 --> 00:00:44,781
The question this film is really asking: what result would prove the claim wrong?

12
00:00:44,801 --> 00:00:49,708
Not right. Results that fit can pile up forever and never finish the job. One result

13
00:00:49,728 --> 00:00:50,940
that doesn't fit can.

14
00:00:51,010 --> 00:00:55,456
Four terms you'll hear. A held-out test set: data kept aside during training, used

15
00:00:55,476 --> 00:01:00,242
only to test the model. Recall: of the real cases, the share the model catches.

16
00:01:00,262 --> 00:01:04,389
Precision: of the cases the model flags, the share that are real. And

17
00:01:04,409 --> 00:01:07,260
out-of-distribution: inputs unlike the data the model learned from.

18
00:01:07,330 --> 00:01:11,694
A dashboard tile says: the system is robust. Under it, an axis: the error rate on

19
00:01:11,714 --> 00:01:16,352
unfamiliar inputs, from none on the left to a lot on the right. Now let results come

20
00:01:16,372 --> 00:01:20,462
in. A low error rate. Robust. A middling one. Still robust. A terrible one. Nobody

21
00:01:20,482 --> 00:01:24,572
wrote down what would count against it, so — still robust. So what would non-robust

22
00:01:24,592 --> 00:01:25,120
look like?

23
00:01:25,190 --> 00:01:28,550
Rewrite it the way the chapter's table does: error rate on out-of-distribution

24
00:01:28,570 --> 00:01:32,493
inputs stays below two percent, across a thirty-day rolling window. Put a mark at

25
00:01:32,513 --> 00:01:36,718
two percent. Everything past it is now forbidden — shade it. Replay the same three

26
00:01:36,738 --> 00:01:40,943
results. The first fits. The second lands in the shaded part. So does the third.

27
00:01:40,963 --> 00:01:45,168
Either one refutes it. The claim can now be wrong, which means it finally says

28
00:01:45,188 --> 00:01:45,450
something.

29
00:01:45,520 --> 00:01:49,166
Second row. The model performs well. The table's rewrite: precision at least point

30
00:01:49,186 --> 00:01:53,395
nine one, and recall at least point eight eight, on the held-out test set, evaluated

31
00:01:53,415 --> 00:01:57,625
monthly. Swap the axis to recall — the share of real cases caught. Watch the

32
00:01:57,645 --> 00:02:01,572
forbidden region move: now it is everything below point eight eight, on the left.

33
00:02:01,592 --> 00:02:05,520
Different claim, different side. Same move: the claim is the region it rules out.

34
00:02:05,590 --> 00:02:09,856
Now the usual way to check a model. Take the sepsis early-warning model the chapter

35
00:02:09,876 --> 00:02:13,571
opens with, and count the evidence that it works. Strong internal validation. A

36
00:02:13,591 --> 00:02:17,285
respectable reported A U C. A risk number on every patient. Published. Cleared

37
00:02:17,305 --> 00:02:21,571
through procurement. Each one pushes confidence up. But look at the top of the bar:

38
00:02:21,591 --> 00:02:25,857
however many you stack, it never reaches certain. Five white swans do not prove that

39
00:02:25,877 --> 00:02:27,000
every swan is white.

40
00:02:27,070 --> 00:02:31,236
So stop asking how much evidence the claim has. Ask what it forbids. The model

41
00:02:31,256 --> 00:02:35,423
performs well — what recall would count against it? Nothing was written down, so the

42
00:02:35,443 --> 00:02:39,609
whole axis is allowed, and every check can only confirm. Now borrow the table's row:

43
00:02:39,629 --> 00:02:43,795
recall at least point eight eight. Everything below it goes dark. That is the claim,

44
00:02:43,815 --> 00:02:45,470
drawn: the outcomes it rules out.

45
00:02:45,540 --> 00:02:49,830
Then a team at the University of Michigan checked the model against what actually

46
00:02:49,850 --> 00:02:52,601
happened to twenty-seven thousand, six hundred ninety-seven hospitalized patients,

47
00:02:52,621 --> 00:02:57,835
at a health system that had not built it. Before the result lands — commit. Where on

48
00:02:57,855 --> 00:03:01,530
this axis does it fall? And what happens to the confidence bar?

49
00:03:01,600 --> 00:03:06,831
It caught roughly one in three. Deep inside the shaded region. And the bar — five

50
00:03:06,851 --> 00:03:10,770
confirmations — falls to nothing. Five white swans. One black one. Settled.

51
00:03:10,840 --> 00:03:15,587
Now the move is quick. Line up the chapter's four claims. Robust becomes: error

52
00:03:15,607 --> 00:03:19,673
below two percent over thirty days. Performs well becomes: precision and recall

53
00:03:19,693 --> 00:03:23,759
floors. The migration was a success becomes: zero data-loss events, and ninety-fifth

54
00:03:23,779 --> 00:03:27,504
percentile latency at most a hundred and twenty milliseconds, forty-eight hours

55
00:03:27,524 --> 00:03:32,271
after cutover. We have mitigated drift becomes: P S I on the three highest-weight

56
00:03:32,291 --> 00:03:36,697
features below point one zero, week over week. Left column: nothing forbidden. Right

57
00:03:36,717 --> 00:03:38,740
column: every cell carves a region.

58
00:03:38,810 --> 00:03:43,176
This deserves its name. A claim is falsifiable when it names the observation that

59
00:03:43,196 --> 00:03:47,248
would make it false. And notice the asymmetry you just watched. Confirming results

60
00:03:47,268 --> 00:03:51,321
pile up without ever reaching certainty. One falsifying result settles it. You can't

61
00:03:51,341 --> 00:03:56,020
prove a model works in all cases. You can prove it fails in this one.

62
00:03:56,090 --> 00:04:00,092
Back to the dashboard. The system is robust. It survived every result because it

63
00:04:00,112 --> 00:04:04,976
forbade none. On a dashboard, a claim that survived a real test and a claim that was

64
00:04:04,996 --> 00:04:08,999
never at risk look identical. Draw the two-percent line, and the same results can

65
00:04:09,019 --> 00:04:13,308
finally say no. Not taught here: writing that line before you read the output. That

66
00:04:13,328 --> 00:04:14,170
part is yours.

67
00:04:14,240 --> 00:04:19,107
Let's recap with Claude. A claim counts only in the form that names the result that

68
00:04:19,127 --> 00:04:23,384
would make it false. Draw it as the outcomes it forbids: robust forbids nothing;

69
00:04:23,404 --> 00:04:27,355
error below two percent over thirty days carves a region. Confirmations pile up

70
00:04:27,375 --> 00:04:31,020
without certainty; one refutation settles it. The sepsis model's checks were white

71
00:04:31,040 --> 00:04:35,296
swans; one external test on twenty-seven thousand patients was the black one. And on

72
00:04:35,316 --> 00:04:37,740
a dashboard, unrefuted and validated look the same.

73
00:04:37,810 --> 00:04:41,706
Your turn. Paste this into Claude: A team reports: Our model achieves 94% accuracy

74
00:04:41,726 --> 00:04:45,623
on the held-out test set. Before anything else, predict: what result would make this

75
00:04:45,643 --> 00:04:49,539
claim false, as written? Then rewrite it the Popperian way, naming a metric, a

76
00:04:49,559 --> 00:04:54,015
threshold and a measurement window, and draw what it forbids as a shaded region on a

77
00:04:54,035 --> 00:04:57,651
number line. Finally, describe one way the model could perform badly that the

78
00:04:57,671 --> 00:05:01,567
original sentence would never catch. Two things to look for. Did it write a

79
00:05:01,587 --> 00:05:06,043
threshold and a window, not just 'accuracy should be high'? And did it say what the

80
00:05:06,063 --> 00:05:09,400
claim forbids before it said anything about whether the claim is true?

81
00:05:09,470 --> 00:05:14,581
A Claim That Cannot Be Wrong Is Not a Claim. At Nik Bear Brown.
